    "summary": "A single strip of hand-woven cotton (Asante kente) made from cotton and rayon. The warp is of stripes of dark blue and white cotton; the weft is of dark blue cotton, in some areas variegated with white. Over this ground weave are supplementary weft float patterns arranged in bands: these include red and yellow bars, and red, yellow and green zigzags, lozenges and stepped forms. The warp ends have been left as a fringe.",
